Subject: [PATCH 03803/11362] [outer-loop] Multi-positive goal induction (lever
 #2): built; re-reaching mechanism DEAD (ARC wins are canonical)

Operator-authorized multi-hour build. Built the full machinery (induce-path win_state_set extension +
gather + cross-positive invariant + discriminative leave-one-out gate; plumbing verified end-to-end on a
mock proposer -- the gate correctly rejects literal-match via perturbation). Decisive CPU finding (no LLM):
ARC-AGI-3 wins are CANONICAL -- re-reaching L1 across diversity-on per-seed paths yields distinct_wins=1 on
EVERY game (lp85/sc25/tu93/vc33), so the "re-reach K times" gather can't produce distinct positives. The
judge's failure-mode-1 is universal -> multi-positive-via-re-reaching is structurally dead.

The K=1 richer-single-encoding fallback (start+delta+invariant+directive vs .430 win-only) hit Qwen
server failures (HTTP 400 / timeout; prompt ~2.8k tokens, not an overflow) -> inconclusive, not worth more
cycles. The canonical-win structure REDIRECTS to lever #4 (mechanic-template): a deterministic goal-predicate
template keyed on the per-game canonical mechanic fits a canonical win far better than fuzzy multi-example
induction; the extension + gate built here are reusable for #4.

Build lives on branch outer-loop/multiwin-goal (commit 6c3e78d64). Note:
docs/research-notes/multiwin-goal-induction-2026-06-24.md.

